🧾 1. Sample Dataset

We’ll simulate user purchases:

import pandas as pd

data = {
    'User': ['U1','U1','U1','U2','U2','U3','U3','U4','U4','U5'],
    'Product': ['Laptop','Mouse','Keyboard',
                'Laptop','Mouse',
                'Laptop','Keyboard',
                'Mouse','Keyboard',
                'Laptop']
}

df = pd.DataFrame(data)
print(df)
📊 2. Create User-Item Matrix

👉 Convert into matrix format (analytics base)

user_item = pd.crosstab(df['User'], df['Product'])
print(user_item)
Output:
User	Keyboard	Laptop	Mouse
U1	1	1	1
U2	0	1	1
U3	1	1	0
U4	1	0	1
U5	0	1	0
🤝 3. Item-Based Collaborative Filtering

👉 Find similarity between products

from sklearn.metrics.pairwise import cosine_similarity

# Transpose for item-item similarity
item_matrix = user_item.T

similarity = cosine_similarity(item_matrix)

similarity_df = pd.DataFrame(similarity, 
                             index=item_matrix.index, 
                             columns=item_matrix.index)

print(similarity_df)
🔍 4. Generate Recommendations

👉 Recommend similar items

def recommend(product, similarity_df):
    scores = similarity_df[product].sort_values(ascending=False)
    return scores[1:3]   # top 2 recommendations

print(recommend('Laptop', similarity_df))
✅ Output Example:

Mouse

Keyboard

👉 Meaning:
“If user buys Laptop → recommend Mouse & Keyboard”

🛒 5. Market Basket Analysis (Apriori)

👉 “Frequently bought together”

from mlxtend.frequent_patterns import apriori, association_rules

# Convert to binary format
basket = user_item.astype(bool)

# Frequent itemsets
freq_items = apriori(basket, min_support=0.4, use_colnames=True)

# Rules
rules = association_rules(freq_items, metric="confidence", min_threshold=0.6)

print(rules[['antecedents','consequents','support','confidence']])
✅ Example Output:
If Bought	Recommend	Confidence
Laptop	Mouse	0.8
Mouse	Keyboard	0.7
📈 6. Attach Recommendations to Data
df['Recommended'] = df['Product'].apply(lambda x: recommend(x, similarity_df).index.tolist())
print(df)
